SOAPBOX: TX Antenna: Cushcraft MA-160V Vertical
SOAPBOX: This was the first contest for the new location in Alabama and even being still a project in motion we had an amazing weekend having fun. Conditions alway for this weekend can make or break it here. Got the to the Station luckily with everything ready to go. The beverage system was not deployed quite yet but will be done here soon enough.
SOAPBOX: Saturday during the day we did some 160m antenna work and the vertical is now on 1900khz and still have not layed any radials on the radial plate. Knew we could use the amplifier there but choose from the start to simply run 100 watts and we did. During Saturday evening we took advantage of the Contest being a learning session which is my goal all the time. We always use Contest weekends as training and team building exercises and this was no different this weekend. Knowing what I need to work on next for this antenna is radials and that will be the field work that may not be so fun but laying the needed long radials will only improve us.
SOAPBOX: 73,
SOAPBOX: Steve KI4KWR
